Package: latchverify
Version: @VERSION@
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.28), libstdc++6, libgcc-s1
Recommends: git, libgtk-3-0t64 | libgtk-3-0, libnss3, libgbm1, libasound2t64 | libasound2, libxss1, libxtst6, libatspi2.0-0t64 | libatspi2.0-0, xdg-utils, libnotify-bin, pkexec | policykit-1
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Homepage: https://github.com/ANI-CPU-tech/LatchVerify
Description: capability-diffing security proxy for MCP servers
 LatchVerify pins Model Context Protocol tool definitions in latch.lock and
 blocks tools/call when a tool gains capabilities without review.
 .
 After installing, run `latch setup` to choose which MCP clients to connect: their servers
 start behind the latch proxy and their tools are pinned in a per-user
 latch.lock. Nothing is connected without your say-so.
 Includes its own Node.js runtime and the LatchVerify desktop app, which needs a
 graphical desktop and the recommended libraries; the latch command needs neither.
